/E (The Automated Vaccine Delivery System is an embedded solution designed to ensure safe and efficient transportation of vaccines with real-time monitoring and minimum human intervention. The main objective of this project is to maintain the required temperature conditions for vaccines during transportation, monitor payload status, and provide live location tracking for effective delivery management. The system uses an Arduino Uno \(ATmega328P\) microcontroller interfaced with a DS18B20 digital temperature sensor to continuously monitor storage temperature, a NEO-6M GPS module for real-time location tracking. Status indications are provided through LED indicators, while a piezo buzzer module alerts users in case of )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (abnormal temperature conditions or delivery issues. The system is powered using a 12V DC power supply with a 5V voltage regulator to ensure stable and reliable operation. This project provides a cost-effective and dependable solution for vaccine transportation and monitoring in healthcare applications. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
