159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 68 0 R
/T (The history of vaccine delivery systems is closely connected to the development of healthcare logistics and cold chain technology. Initially, vaccines were transported manually using insulated containers with ice packs, and temperature monitoring relied entirely on human supervision. These traditional methods were time-consuming and often unreliable, resulting in vaccine spoilage due to improper storage conditions.  During the late 20th century, electronic temperature monitoring devices  were introduced to improve vaccine storage and transportation safety. Basic  refrigeration systems and digital thermometers helped maintain controlled  temperatures during delivery. However, these systems still lacked real-time  monitoring and tracking capabilities. )
/E (The history of vaccine delivery systems is closely connected to the development of healthcare logistics and cold chain technology. Initially, vaccines were transported manually using insulated containers with ice packs, and temperature monitoring relied entirely on human supervision. These traditional methods were time-consuming and often unreliable, resulting in vaccine spoilage due to improper storage conditions.  During the late 20th century, electronic temperature monitoring devices  were introduced to improve vaccine storage and transportation safety. Basic  refrigeration systems and digital thermometers helped maintain controlled  temperatures during delivery. However, these systems still lacked real-time  monitoring and tracking capabilities. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 68 0 R
/T ( An Automated Vaccine Delivery System is a modern technological solution designed to ensure the safe transportation and monitoring of vaccines during delivery. The system continuously monitors critical parameters such as storage temperature, payload weight, and delivery location, which are essential for maintaining vaccine quality and effectiveness. Sensors and tracking modules are connected to a microcontroller that collects and processes data in real time.  In traditional vaccine transportation, monitoring is done manually, which  may lead to temperature fluctuations, improper handling, delayed deliveries,  and vaccine wastage. Maintaining the vaccine cold chain is one of the major  challenges in healthcare logistics. The automated vaccine delivery system  overcomes these limitations by providing real-time monitoring, automated  alerts, and accurate tracking throughout the transportation process.  The system uses an Arduino-based embedded platform integrated with  temperature sensors, GPS tracking modules, LED indicators, and buzzer alerts.)
/E ( An Automated Vaccine Delivery System is a modern technological solution designed to ensure the safe transportation and monitoring of vaccines during delivery. The system continuously monitors critical parameters such as storage temperature, payload weight, and delivery location, which are essential for maintaining vaccine quality and effectiveness. Sensors and tracking modules are connected to a microcontroller that collects and processes data in real time.  In traditional vaccine transportation, monitoring is done manually, which  may lead to temperature fluctuations, improper handling, delayed deliveries,  and vaccine wastage. Maintaining the vaccine cold chain is one of the major  challenges in healthcare logistics. The automated vaccine delivery system  overcomes these limitations by providing real-time monitoring, automated  alerts, and accurate tracking throughout the transportation process.  The system uses an Arduino-based embedded platform integrated with  temperature sensors, GPS tracking modules, LED indicators, and buzzer alerts.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
