/P 69 0 R
/T (and 2010s, modern vaccine delivery systems began incorporating GPS tracking, wireless communication, and automated monitoring features.  These systems enabled healthcare providers to track vaccine transportation  in real time and receive alerts whenever storage conditions became unsafe. Today, automated vaccine delivery systems use smart sensors, cloud-based monitoring, and intelligent analytics to improve vaccine transportation efficiency, reduce wastage, and support large-scale immunization programs. This evolution has transformed vaccine logistics into a safer, more reliable, and technology-driven process. )
/E (and 2010s, modern vaccine delivery systems began incorporating GPS tracking, wireless communication, and automated monitoring features.  These systems enabled healthcare providers to track vaccine transportation  in real time and receive alerts whenever storage conditions became unsafe. Today, automated vaccine delivery systems use smart sensors, cloud-based monitoring, and intelligent analytics to improve vaccine transportation efficiency, reduce wastage, and support large-scale immunization programs. This evolution has transformed vaccine logistics into a safer, more reliable, and technology-driven process. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
