203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 70 0 R
/T (depends mainly on manual checking and traditional cold storage methods. Healthcare workers must physically inspect temperature conditions and delivery status, which is time-consuming and often inaccurate.  There is no continuous real-time monitoring of vaccine temperature or  transportation conditions. Delays in delivery or unexpected temperature  variations can damage vaccines and reduce their effectiveness. Lack of  proper tracking also makes it difficult to monitor delivery routes and ensure  timely transportation. Managing vaccine transportation manually increases  operational costs, human effort, and the possibility of vaccine wastage. )
/E (depends mainly on manual checking and traditional cold storage methods. Healthcare workers must physically inspect temperature conditions and delivery status, which is time-consuming and often inaccurate.  There is no continuous real-time monitoring of vaccine temperature or  transportation conditions. Delays in delivery or unexpected temperature  variations can damage vaccines and reduce their effectiveness. Lack of  proper tracking also makes it difficult to monitor delivery routes and ensure  timely transportation. Managing vaccine transportation manually increases  operational costs, human effort, and the possibility of vaccine wastage. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 70 0 R
/T (Traditional vaccine transportation methods rely heavily on manual supervision and periodic monitoring, which can lead to vaccine spoilage, delayed deliveries, and improper handling. Maintaining the required storage temperature throughout transportation is a major challenge, especially in remote areas and long-distance deliveries.  In many cases, healthcare workers cannot continuously monitor vaccine  conditions or accurately track the delivery vehicle in real time. Sudden  temperature fluctuations, handling errors, or delays may reduce vaccine  effectiveness and increase wastage. Manual monitoring also requires  significant human effort and may not provide immediate alerts during  emergencies.  Therefore, there is a need for an automated, reliable, and cost-effective  system that can continuously monitor vaccine transportation conditions,  provide real-time location tracking, and generate alerts whenever unsafe  conditions occur. The automated vaccine delivery system addresses these  challenges by integrating sensors, GPS technology, and embedded systems  to improve vaccine safety and transportation efficiency. )
/E (Traditional vaccine transportation methods rely heavily on manual supervision and periodic monitoring, which can lead to vaccine spoilage, delayed deliveries, and improper handling. Maintaining the required storage temperature throughout transportation is a major challenge, especially in remote areas and long-distance deliveries.  In many cases, healthcare workers cannot continuously monitor vaccine  conditions or accurately track the delivery vehicle in real time. Sudden  temperature fluctuations, handling errors, or delays may reduce vaccine  effectiveness and increase wastage. Manual monitoring also requires  significant human effort and may not provide immediate alerts during  emergencies.  Therefore, there is a need for an automated, reliable, and cost-effective  system that can continuously monitor vaccine transportation conditions,  provide real-time location tracking, and generate alerts whenever unsafe  conditions occur. The automated vaccine delivery system addresses these  challenges by integrating sensors, GPS technology, and embedded systems  to improve vaccine safety and transportation efficiency. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
