754 0 obj
<<
/Title (An Automated Vaccine Delivery System is a modern technological solution designed to ensure the safe transportation and monitoring of vaccines during delivery. The system continuously monitors critical parameters such as storage temperature, payload weight, and delivery location, which are essential for maintaining vaccine quality and effectiveness. Sensors and tracking modules are connected to a microcontroller that collects and processes data in real time.  In traditional vaccine transportation, monitoring is done manually, which  may lead to temperature fluctuations, improper handling, delayed deliveries,  and vaccine wastage. Maintaining the vaccine cold chain is one of the major  challenges in healthcare logistics. The automated vaccine delivery system  overcomes these limitations by providing real-time monitoring, automated  alerts, and accurate tracking throughout the transportation process.  The system uses an Arduino-based embedded platform integrated with  temperature sensors, GPS tracking modules, LED indicators, and buzzer alerts.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 749 0 R
/Next 766 0 R
>>
endobj
