/Title (The history of vaccine delivery systems is closely connected to the development of healthcare logistics and cold chain technology. Initially, vaccines were transported manually using insulated containers with ice packs, and temperature monitoring relied entirely on human supervision. These traditional methods were time-consuming and often unreliable, resulting in vaccine spoilage due to improper storage conditions.  During the late 20th century, electronic temperature monitoring devices  were introduced to improve vaccine storage and transportation safety. Basic  refrigeration systems and digital thermometers helped maintain controlled  temperatures during delivery. However, these systems still lacked real-time  monitoring and tracking capabilities.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 755 0 R
>>
endobj
